{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLqgXXr7NRJUn751VbB2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fixed: `limit(2**(1/x), x, 0, dir='-')` now returns `0`. The right-hand limit is still `oo`.\n\n**Cause:** In `sympy/series/limits.py`, the fallback `pow_heuristics` used for powers calculated its inner limits without passing the direction on. So a left-hand limit was quietly worked out from the default right-hand side, which gave `oo`.\n\n**Fix:** `pow_heuristics` now takes a `dir` argument and passes it to each of its inner `limit` calls. The one place that calls it (in `doit`) now passes `dir` in.\n\n**Second example:** on this checkout, `limit(2**x, x, -oo)` already returned `0` before my change, so I couldn't reproduce that part of the report. It still returns `0`, and `limit(x**(1/x), x, oo)` still returns `1`.\n\n**Tests:** `sympy/series/tests/test_limits.py` and `test_gruntz.py` pass: 211 passed, 3 skipped, 6 expected failures."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":480,"cache_read_input_tokens":21050,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":480},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"adb7d843-f221-4dd8-9f74-74f4f6fdc59b","uuid":"93462f3a-5812-4ded-8192-4ef681227c1a","timestamp":"2026-11-24T00:54:07.391Z","request_id":"req_011ChLqgX8YXwtVjQWU3Pv7Z"}
